Court is only allowed to consider arguments made in court and documents filed by actual parties to the case. They cannot ethically read or consider any other opinions or arguments about the case, and they cannot give legal advice. Thank you. Current Assignment Previous Assignments Office Judicial Assistant Division Procedures Education Statewide Committees and Appointments Current Assignment Circuit Court Judge, August 2025 – Present Alachua: Family Division DR1 1/5 Division “DV” (Domestic Violence) Baker: Domestic Violence Family Juvenile Dependency Mental Health Probate Previous Assignments Alachua County Court Judge, September 2017 – August 2025 Alachua: County Criminal Division III (O-Z) Alachua County Canvassing Board Alachua: Civil Traffic Alachua County Civil Division V Alachua Criminal: Back-up Coverage Weeks 1 & 3 (Monday and Tuesday ONLY) Alachua: Mental Health, Division S Circuit-wide Back-up Coverage Weeks 1 & 3 Baker: Appeals Circuit Civil Juvenile Delinquency Mortgage Foreclosures Extraordinary Writs Office Alachua County Family and Civil Justice Center 201 East University Avenue, Room 301 Gainesville, FL 32601 Phone: (352) 374-3644 Baker County Courthouse 339 East Macclenny Avenue Macclenny, FL 32063 Phone: (904) 259-4705 Fax: (904) 259-0218 Judicial Assistant Amber Allen email: AllenA@circuit8.org Phone: (352) 374-3644 Division Procedures Judge Van Vorst’s Division Procedures Education Juris Doctor with Honors: University of Florida College of Law, 2002 Bachelor of Arts with Highest Honors: Business Administration, University of Florida, 1999 Statewide Committees and Appointments Trial Court Budget Commission, Executive Committee, and Budget Management Committee Subgroup Workload Assessment Advisory Committee, Vice-Chair Judicial Management Council Workgroup on Trial Court Technology Strategies and Funding Subgroup Florida Bar Civil Rules Committee Faculty: Conference of County Court Judges, Florida Judicial College, and Advanced Judicial Studies Cri